  "id": "evaluator",
  "term": "evaluator",
  "definition": "In this embodied-cognition model, an evaluator is one of three proposed cognitive dyads and refers to a pattern of sensorimotor functioning involved in how actions are controlled and perceived. The evaluator is described as part of normal social attunement in the model, while an extreme evaluator is proposed as a form of mis-attunement linked to psychiatric difficulties.",
